This project is an independent implementation inspired by LightAgent
(https://github.com/wanxingai/LightAgent), licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
Studied reference: commit f8083ab03badffe3331bfc0d35e3ac6dab6812c8 (version 1.0.0).
The code here is written from scratch.

Ideas taken from LightAgent that Trellis implements:
  - structured per-run trace events with an aggregate summary;
  - validating tool-call arguments against JSON Schema and reporting errors back to the model;
  - deterministic, assertion-based regression evaluation of outputs, tool use and cost,
    run with fake models in CI;
  - pinning GitHub Actions to commit SHAs (the pinned SHAs in .github/workflows/ci.yml
    were copied from LightAgent's workflow file).

Ideas taken from LightAgent that are planned for later milestones (not implemented yet):
  - dependency-graph validation by topological sort, and fail-fast / continue-independent
    failure policies, for task scheduling;
  - write-admission checks on long-term memory (such as duplicate rejection and write limits).

Studied but not adopted: verification-gated task artifacts, lease-based persistent scheduling,
and event-sourced session storage.
